The Shakti patrol began pulling uphill once it became clear they no longer held the track. Tiger Squad followed. Allowing anyone to reach the plateau with a description of an armed PAPER unit below Sublime Point would make the remaining climb considerably harder.\
That part of the engagement was short.\
By the time firing stopped, the Shakti patrol was no longer capable of reporting anything.\
Tiger Squad remained capable of continuing, but only after revising what constituted Tiger Squad.\
They recovered who they could reach and treated the wounded where they lay before moving them off the route. Some injuries could be dressed and carried further. Others could not be reconciled with several hundred metres of steep climbing. The dead were searched for identification, weapons and anything PAPER could not afford to have found with them, then concealed under rock and scrub away from the path. The wounded who could not continue were moved together into cover with medical supplies, food, water and weapons.\
One argued that he could still climb.\
His leg disagreed more convincingly.\
The team reduced packs, abandoned what could be replaced, and redistributed what could not. The second rifles were redistributed among fewer people. So were the packs.\
When they moved again, they left dead colleagues, wounded colleagues and most of a Shakti patrol behind them beneath the cliffs.\
Tiger Squad turned uphill.\

